# The health check. Read by scripts/gen_launchd.py.

[job]
name = watchdog
exit_timeout = 120
run_at_load = false

[program]
{VENV_PYTHON}
{ROOT}/agent/watchdog.py
--once

[environment]
TZ = America/New_York
PATH = /usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin
AGENTIC_TRADING_ROOT = {ROOT}

[schedule]
# The trading day, at the same rate as the loop it is watching.
every 5 minutes from 09:25 to 16:05 on weekdays
# The rest of the weekday, on the hour. Gateway falls over overnight as often as
# it does at lunchtime, and finding out at 09:25 is finding out too late.
hourly from 00:00 to 08:00 on weekdays
hourly from 17:00 to 23:00 on weekdays
# All day at the weekend.
hourly from 00:00 to 23:00 on weekends

[comment]
The health check, run by launchd.

It runs one pass of agent/watchdog.py, which looks at whether IB Gateway is up,
whether the market data feed is still delivering prices, whether the trading
loop has written a recent heartbeat, and how much free disk space is left. If
any of them is wrong it tells Mo.

Every five minutes from 09:25 to 16:05 on weekdays, which is the window the
trading loop is awake in, and once an hour the rest of the time including all
day Saturday and Sunday. That is 533 wake ups a week.

What it is allowed to do: if Gateway is down it may restart Gateway, once, and
then it leaves it alone. That is the only thing it changes. It never places an
order, never changes one, never cancels one. It looks and it tells you.

Load this one before the tick job. It is the thing that tells you the loop has
stopped, so it is not much use arriving second.
